        "competenceGoal": "Students learn the basics of scientific work in the form of literature research, writing a scientific paper and giving a\npresentation to a specialist audience.\nLearning objectives:\nStudents learn to read conference papers, articles in specialist journals and standard literature. Furthermore, they\ninterpret these texts in order to give an overview of the topic in their own words in a paper. Finally, they also present an\noverview of the topic to other computer scientists. In doing so, they are trained in scientific writing in the form of\nexpression, text structure and reduction to the essentials.\nStudents are familiar with the DFG Code of Conduct \"Guidelines for Safeguarding Good Scientific Practice\" and\nsuccessfully apply these guidelines when writing their scientific work.",
        "content": "This module bundles the seminars at the Chair of Embedded Systems:\nInternt of Things\nMachine Learning\nEmbedded Security and Architectures\nFor current information, please check the course catalog and the Chair of Embedded Systems homepage at https://\nces.itec.kit.edu.",
