      "M-PHYS-102121": {
        "id": "M-PHYS-102121",
        "title": "Detectors for Particle and Astroparticle Physics, with ext. Exercises",
        "credits": 8,
        "term": "WS",
        "termString": "Each winter term",
        "duration": "1 term",
        "language": "English",
        "grading": "graded",
        "coordinators": [
          "PD Dr. Frank Hartmann",
          "Prof. Dr. Markus Klute"
        ],
        "organisation": "KIT Department of Physics",
        "partOf": [],
        "categories": [
          "Electives"
        ],
        "applicableSpecializations": [],
        "isLab": false,
        "isThesis": false,
        "examType": "Oral Exam. In the MSc Physics, this module is examined together with further modules attended as part of the major in\nphysics. The total duration of the oral exam is approx. 60 minutes.",
        "prerequisites": "none",
        "modeledPrerequisites": "The following conditions have to be fulfilled:\n1.\nThe module M-PHYS-102119 - Detectors for Particle and Astroparticle Physics, without ext. Exercises must not have\n2.\n3.\nbeen started.\nThe module M-PHYS-102120 - Detectors for Particle and Astroparticle Physics, without ext. Exercises (Minor) must\nnot have been started.\nThe module M-PHYS-102122 - Detectors for Particle and Astroparticle Physics, with ext. Exercises (Minor) must not\nhave been started.",
        "exclusions": [],
        "requires": [],
        "competenceGoal": "Advanced study in one area of experimental particle and astroparticle physics. Students learn experimental aspects of\nmeasuring particle properties. Thus, they learn the basics for a detailed analysis of experimental data, the operation of\ncomplex experiments and the work with modern particle detectors. The practical exercises introduce the students to\nexperimental work with detectors in teams. In extended exercises, basic principles of sensors and their design optimization\nare simulated on the computer.",
        "content": "Interaction of electrons, photons, muons, charged and neutral hadrons with matter; electronic detection of particle\nradiation and measurement of deposited energy and particle identification; gas-filled detectors, scintillators,\nphotomultipliers, silicon detectors, electromagnetic and hadronic calorimeters, detector systems, triggers and data\nacquisition, reconstruction of physical objects in detector systems, applications outside basic research.",
        "workload": "240 hours, of which attendance time (60 hours). The remaining hours are used for preparation for the experiments,\npreparation of practical protocols, follow-up of the lecture material and preparation for the examination (180 hours).",
        "recommendations": "Basic knowledge of experimental nuclear and particle physics, e.g. from the lecture Modern Experimental Physics III in the\nbachelor's program in physics. Basic knowledge of electronics is also helpful.\nPhysics Master (Master of Science)\n4 MODULES Module: Detectors for Particle and Astroparticle Physics, with ext. Exercises [M-PHYS-102121]",
        "literature": ""
      },
