      "M-PHYS-106323": {
        "id": "M-PHYS-106323",
        "title": "Introduction to Neutron Scattering",
        "credits": 6,
        "term": "WS+SS",
        "termString": "Irregular",
        "duration": "1 term",
        "language": "English",
        "grading": "graded",
        "coordinators": [
          "PD Dr. Frank Weber"
        ],
        "organisation": "KIT Department of Physics",
        "partOf": [],
        "categories": [
          "Electives"
        ],
        "applicableSpecializations": [],
        "isLab": false,
        "isThesis": false,
        "examType": "Zur Verwendung als Schwerpunktfach/Ergänzungsfach:\nMündliche Prüfung. Im Rahmen des Schwerpunktfachs des MSc Physik wird das Modul zusammen mit weiteren belegten\nModulen geprüft. Die Dauer der mündlichen Prüfung beträgt insgesamt ca. 60 Minuten.",
        "prerequisites": "None",
        "modeledPrerequisites": "",
        "exclusions": [],
        "requires": [],
        "competenceGoal": "The students understand the theoretical and technical basic principles of neutron scattering experiments. For a specific\nscientific question, the students are able to evaluate various neutron scattering techniques and select the best-suited one.\nStudent are able to critically read and assess scientific publications based on neutron scattering techniques.",
        "content": "This lecture familiarizes the students with the basic principles of neutron scattering, the theoretical description and\nexperimental realization of neutron scattering experiments. We will discuss methods for structure determination and\nimaging based on nuclear and magnetic scattering mechanisms. Applications to investigate lattice and magnetic degrees of\nfreedom discussed along with a short introduction to second quantization formalism and linear response theory. An\noverview and short comparison of complementary scattering methods (x-ray, electron) is given. The lecture will be\nillustrated with examples from current work on quantum materials.\n• Basics of the neutron-matter interaction\n• Concepts for the theoretical description of neutron scattering\n• Production and detection of neutrons\n• Structure determination with neutrons\n• Inelastic neutron scattering – neutron spectroscopy\n• Introduction: 2nd quantization, linear response\n• Complementary scattering techniques",
        "workload": "(135 hours).\n180 hours, composed of attendance time (45 hours), wrap-up of the lecture, working on the exercises and exam preparation",
        "recommendations": "expected.\nBasic knowledge of condensed matter physics, quantum mechanics, as well as thermodynamics and statistical physics are",
        "literature": ""
      },
