        "exclusions": [],
        "requires": [],
        "competenceGoal": "Students know and understand advanced mathematical methods and are able to apply them to construct approximate\nsolutions of practical problems in theoretical physics.",
        "content": "Perturbation theory and asymptotic expansions for obtaining analytic solutions to ordinary and differential equations and\nintegrals. Such topics as behaviour of differential equations close to singular points, WKB approximation, large orders of\nperturbations theory, summation of series, asymptotic expansion of integrals, Green’s functions for ordinary and partial\ndifferential equations, boundary layer theory etc. will be discussed.",
        "workload": "h)\n360 h consisting of attendance time (90 h), wrap-up of the lecture incl. exam preparation and working on the exercises (270",
        "recommendations": "The course is suitable for students at both bachelor and master level who are interested in theoretical physics.",
